    "en": {
      "caveats": "The text is an introductory essay to a special issue and does not present empirical data or a specific localized case study.",
      "what": "This introductory paper establishes a framework for analyzing science fiction through a geographical lens, focusing on how the genre uses fictional displacement and deterritorialization to represent spatial relationships. It introduces a special issue dedicated to exploring the unique spatial affordances of science fiction texts in the context of contemporary planetary crises.",
      "why": "It bridges a gap between literary studies and geography, offering researchers a theoretical basis to use speculative fiction as a tool for analyzing and rethinking human relationships to threatened environments."
